Found by the coordinator while parent-reviewing B011, 2026-08-24, immediately
after B015/GH #60 merged. Reproduced on master @ 4871431 with the release binary.

## The false positive
A declaration whose ONLY callers live in omitted own-module files is reported
"never used". The game compiles those files, so the warning is wrong.

Via gitignore (default-on since GH #60 — no config needed):

    info.toml, .gitignore = "generated/"
    src/Main.as        void UsedOnlyByGenerated() {}
    generated/Gen.as   void GenCaller() { UsedOnlyByGenerated(); }

    $ openplanet-lsp check .
    src/Main.as:2:1: warning: a function `UsedOnlyByGenerated` is never used

`--no-gitignore` clears it (and correctly reports `GenCaller` instead).

## It PREDATES GH #60 — verified
The identical FP reproduces with no gitignore anywhere, via `ignore_paths`:

    .openplanet-lsp.toml   ignore_paths = ["gen2"]
    src/Main.as            void UsedOnlyByIgnored() {}
    gen2/Gen.as            void GenCaller() { UsedOnlyByIgnored(); }
    -> src/Main.as:2:1: warning: a function `UsedOnlyByIgnored` is never used

So the defect is: **the unused-declaration usage join treats the VISIBLE file set
as the whole compile set.** GH #60 did not introduce it; it made an existing hole
reachable with no configuration, which is what raises the priority.

## Design: include omitted own-module files for USAGE RECORDING ONLY
Omitted own-module files should be parsed and fed to the usage-collection pass,
but must NOT contribute declarations to the pooled symbol table and must NOT
report diagnostics. `WorkspaceSourceFile.report_diagnostics` already models
"contributes symbols only" for dependency exports; this needs the complement —
"contributes usage only".

Failure direction is correct: usage from a stale gitignored copy can MASK a
genuine unused warning (a missed warning), which repo culture accepts, rather
than manufacturing a bogus one.

### Two alternatives, both refuted by measurement (do not revisit without new evidence)
1. **Parse omitted files fully into the table** (the obvious fix) — REFUTED.
   Gitignored dirs in the real fleet are predominantly whole-tree COPIES
   (`.worktrees/`, `.scratch/research/lsp-probe/` — 26 and 22 files in
   tm-control-mcp and tm-tournament-station). Probe: with a copy of
   `src/Main.as` under `.worktrees/copy/`, `--no-gitignore` reports `Helper`
   unused in BOTH trees even though each tree's `Boot()` calls it — duplicate
   declarations break usage attribution, doubling and misattributing warnings.
   This is exactly the noise GH #60 removed (tm-control-mcp 107 -> 35 warnings).
2. **Disarm the unused pass whenever any own-module file is omitted** — REFUTED.
   It would disable a shipped feature on every plugin that configures
   `source_paths`/`ignore_paths`, which is many of them. A rule that goes
   vacuously silent on real projects is worse than the FP.

## Scope note
Locals/parameters (B011) are NOT exposed: a local's usage is bounded by its own
function body, so no other file can affect it. This is the file-level and
class-member declaration pass only.

The GH #58 namespace rule is a DIFFERENT hole with the same cause, already fenced
separately on the B013 branch (authority disarms when files were omitted).
Design (f) here does not restore its authority — declarations stay invisible — so
that fence remains correct and must not be removed.

## Test plan (TDD, red first)
Red: the two probes above, as fixture tests — a gitignored caller and an
`ignore_paths` caller must both leave the callee unwarned. Variants: caller in a
`source_paths`-excluded dir; caller inside a nested `.gitignore`; usage via
member access / type position / `import` alias rather than a call; a declaration
used ONLY by a gitignored copy of itself (must not warn — masked, per the accepted
direction); a genuinely unused declaration with omitted files present (must STILL
warn, so the fix does not silently disarm the pass); class-member and enum-value
usage from an omitted file; `honor_gitignore = false` unchanged.
Guard: assert omitted files produce ZERO diagnostics of their own (no squiggles
in gitignored files — the GH #60 goal must survive).

GitHub issue: https://github.com/clankercode/lsp-openplanet/issues/61 (gh-61), filed 2026-08-24 with both repros and the two refuted alternatives.


2026-08-24 laneA-unused progress (worktree .worktrees/gh61-usage-only, branch
fix/usage-only-omitted-files, 3 commits on master 4a3b5c4):

* eb79bfd red tests + inert plumbing. Both repros reproduced as tests, exact
  issue wording: "src/Main.as:1:1: warning: a function `UsedOnlyByOmitted` is
  never used". 9 in-memory cases red, 4 CLI end-to-end red, controls green.
* 7a8517b green. `WorkspaceUsage::collect` records usage from
  `snapshot.usage_only_sources()`.
* 0d9d0c6 README + CHANGELOG.

Design as specified (usage recording only), with ONE addition worth flagging:
the pass runs against a SCRATCH symbol table — pooled symbols plus the omitted
files' NON-COLLIDING declarations, file_ids past the end of the snapshot, alive
for one function, never seen by the join. Without their own declarations an
omitted file's body does not resolve, so a generated subclass calling an
inherited member (`class Derived : Base` ... `Hook()`) records nothing and the
FP survives. The collision filter came out of a red test, not taste: with both
`Dead`s in the table a stale copy's own `Dead()` call records nothing and the
masking that stops whole-tree copies manufacturing warnings is lost — refuted
alternative 1's defect in miniature. Skipping any decl the pooled table already
has means a pure copy adds nothing and resolves against the originals, while a
genuinely new decl still goes in.

Evidence: 849 lib + 60 cli_check tests, 0 failures. Clippy 56 `--> src`
warnings, one FEWER than baseline, none in touched files. Both release-binary
repros now clean; `--no-gitignore` unchanged (still reports `GenCaller`).
Fleet dogfood over 153 real plugin roots: exactly ONE delta, tm-music-mania
63 -> 62 warnings, a textbook true positive — `AddTurboToAudioPackRegistry` is
declared in src/PackRegistry.as and its only caller is OtherPacks/TurboAssets.as,
which `source_paths = ["src"]` excludes. Zero new warnings anywhere in the fleet.
Perf: unchanged when nothing is omitted (262-file plugin 0.50s -> 0.46s); worst
case with a gitignored whole-tree copy beside it 0.53s -> 0.74s, proportional to
the omitted count.

GH #58 fence untouched: `dependency_closure_complete` still gates on the
omission, and `usage_only_sources_do_not_restore_namespace_authority` pins it.

Independent ccc review launched, verdict pending.

